      <notesStmt>
        <note>This article analyzes the position of the manuscript Vat. lat. 11600 in the tradition of the Latin translation of Proclus' commentary on Parmenides by Guillaume de Moerbeke. The author notes that «A semble être plus proche de y puisqu'il partage avec y quelques fautes importantes» but still produces a trifid stemma, while it then would make more sense to attach x and y to the same hyparchetype and produce a bifid stemma.</note>
      </notesStmt>
